  "mach:judgement": "Adopt",
  "mach:judgementReason": "The foundational medical image segmentation and registration toolkit — underpins 3D Slicer, ITK-SNAP, and numerous imaging AI pipelines. Apache 2.0, v5.4.6 released May 2026, 1.6k stars, 728 forks, NumFOCUS-sponsored. Cross-platform C++ with Python bindings. Like dcm4che in the DICOM space, ITK is infrastructure that often operates invisibly inside other tools rather than being directly deployed by end users.",
  "mach:editorialReviewedAt": "2026-05-14",
